Fedora-only fix-up, kept here on purpose: this repository builds its own package, kernel-surface-cmdrshepardspie
(see pins.conf), which installs beside linux-surface's kernel-surface and must never replace or remove it. It
changes linux-surface's own Fedora packaging patches (pkg/fedora/kernel-surface/patches):
- 0003: drops "Conflicts:/Obsoletes: kernel-surface < 6.3.6-1". Under the new name those lines would act on
  linux-surface's own package (old versions only, but an Obsoletes of another project's package is never ours
  to ship). Its other lines name %{package_name}, which is now this repository's own name, so they stay.
- 0004: dropped. Its kernel-surface-cmdrshepardspie-default-watchdog would install the same files as
  linux-surface's kernel-surface-default-watchdog (so the two can't both be installed), and the kernel
  Recommends it, so dnf pulls it in. It makes each newly installed Surface kernel the default; these kernels
  carry only Red Hat's test signature until they are signed on the machine, so with Secure Boot on that makes
  an unbootable kernel the default. Without it, Fedora's own rules (UPDATEDEFAULT in /etc/sysconfig/kernel)
  decide.
- 0005: the same Recommends: intel-vsc-firmware line, with 0004's line gone from its context.
This version fits the packaging patches as rebased onto kernel-7.3.0-65's spec (CONTRIB 7.3-pro9).
